#23219
&07A Corridor in Sietch Tabr&00~
You hear a low babble of voices, all speaking at once.  The walls of this place
seem to reflect the sound, so that you cannot determine the location.  A sheet
of dull, rock colored canvas cover a door to the west here.  A solid looking
stone door to the south has strange markings on it.  The odors of this place
assail you, unwashed bodies, distillate esthers of unreclaimed wastes,
everywhere the sour effluvia of humanity with, over all of it, a turbulence of
the spice melange.    
~
